A||||8||mshill||What to look for on T-tops?||||5||
Z||000000||mshill||07-31-2000||12:31 PM||||I will be looking at an 87GT with T-tops this evening.  I want to know what it is that I need to check to make sure the tops and seals are in decent condition?  Also,  are there parts that cannot be replaced if missing or worn?<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Raydar||07-31-2000||01:38 PM||||Look around in the car for evidence of any leaks. Rust on the seat bolts. Stains on the headliner or carpet. If your seller doesn't mind, spray the tops with a hose. Don't use a nozzle, or you *will* force water past the seals. <BR>Look for missing/broken parts. The holes in the "A" pillar and "B" pillar caps will break, if the roof panels are latched before the glass is all the way down on the seal. The fuzzy seals (P-seals) along the front and back of the opening are major wear areas. As a worst case, there will be a strip of aluminum with no padding at all. There are replacements available. <BR>As far as I know, there are NO replacements available for the weather stripping on the drivers's side. This is the strip that starts by the mirror, goes up the A pillar, around the opening, and down the B pillar. <BR>T-tops are cool, but most new replacement parts, if you can find them, are obscenely expensive. Rebuild kits for the mechanisms are available and fairly reasonable. Good luck!<P>------------------<P>Raydar<BR>88 Formula T-Top <BR>88 Coupe (ISO 3800)<P>"Some mornings, it just isn't worth<BR>chewing through the restraints."<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 07-31-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||GT Bastard||07-31-2000||01:53 PM||||'87 w/t-tops??????????||||reg||5
Z||000003||Raydar||07-31-2000||01:59 PM||||T-tops were installed in some pre 88 cars. They were considered a dealer or aftermarket option. The 88 T-top cars were shipped directly from the factory to C&C, for conversion. There wasn't an RPO code (CJB) until 88. <BR>AFAIK, C&C manufactured all the kits. <P>------------------<BR><BR>Raydar<BR>88 Formula T-Top <BR>88 Coupe (ISO 3800)<P>"Some mornings, it just isn't worth<BR>chewing through the restraints."||||reg||1
Z||000004||RobertVol||07-31-2000||02:02 PM||||there are a few 87 with t tops GT. But were not from sold from the dealer. usually they were put in from C&C at a later date. Or someone bought the kit and put them in themselves. Look at P seals, AND the Back Black frame running accross the back on the roof. I forget the name but look at the corners and push down. If loose or you see alot of movement ....Bad sign! I have 2 with T's do trust me on this ! Been there and done that <P>------------------<BR>Robert<BR>88GT Top 3.8 SC t top <BR>88GT T top 55k for sale<BR>  <A HREF="http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros" TARGET=_blank>http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros</A>  <BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fortunecity.com/marina/strand/1086/3eab6a20.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Standard||07-31-2000||02:02 PM||||C&C put aftermarket T-Tops on a lot of different Fiero's.. the only thing special about the 88's is that it has a factory option code on the RPO sheet.<P>------------------<BR>Mike -- Golden Valley, MN<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 148,000 miles and counting!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||007DOUG||07-31-2000||10:46 PM||||"p" seals are no problem, they are available. "p" seals keep out dust/dirt only. they have nothing to do with water leakage<P>If the rubber gaskets are bad, you're screwed. They aren't available anymore.<P>I'm with Raydar, I love my T's, but they continue to cost me dearly....long after the intial purchase price.<P>------------------<BR><I>"Time is simultaneously my most precious and most perishable of all my possessions."</I>||||reg||6
Z||000007||RobertVol||07-31-2000||11:12 PM||||Thanks for clearing me up. I didnt clarify that. The p seal are not for leakage but when they start showing their age they are really tacky looking. Its a cosmetic thing and you would have to be the judge whether important or not||||reg||1
Z||000008||Raydar||08-01-2000||12:18 AM||||For the "non-purist" T-top owners.<BR>Several folks have suggested that, instead of replacing the P-seals, just remove the "remains" of the old ones. (I believe you will need to reinstall the rivets in the trim.) Then buy several feet of black plastic door-edge molding, -the kind with adhesive in the channel, -and put it on the exposed front and back edges of the glass. Should provide a finished look, and fill the gaps between the glass and the trim.<BR>Just my $.02<P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR>88 Formula T-Top <BR>88 Coupe (ISO big V-6)<P>"Some mornings, it just isn't worth<BR>chewing through the restraints."||||reg||1
